The documents of P203's oracle test (scripts/check_json.py), which holds
paslang's JSON parser and writer to Go's encoding/json/v2.

suite/    JSONTestSuite's test_parsing, the 318 files as published at
          https://github.com/nst/JSONTestSuite, commit
          1ef36fa01286573e846ac449e8683f8833c5b26a (2024-11-22), MIT
          License (suite/LICENSE): y_ files are JSON, n_ files are not,
          i_ files are for each parser to decide. Where paslang differs
          from the suite's y_ files it is I-JSON (RFC 7493): a name twice
          in an object and a noncharacter are refused (the MANUAL's
          chapter on JSON lists each i_ verdict).
corpus/   Go's test corpus of encoding/json (golang/src/encoding/json/
          internal/jsontest/_embed/*.json.zst), as Go's repository holds
          it, under Go's license (LICENSE-GO in the tree's root); read
          with Python's compression.zstd, for the tests only.
oracle.go Go's side: built by check_json.py with go build when Go is on
          the machine (a test tool, never a build one).
expect.txt What both sides write, paslang's on purpose different only
          where a noncharacter is refused: check_json.py --update
          writes it from Go's output, checked line by line.
